            <ArticleTitle>Use of lipid-lowering medication in patients with acute myocardial infarction (Worcester Heart Attack Study).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1095-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As part of a population-based longitudinal study, we examined the use of lipid-lowering medication in 3,824 patients hospitalized with acute myocardial infarction in the Worcester, Massachusetts metropolitan area between 1986 and 1993. The rate of utilization of lipid-lowering medication either before (1.8%) or during hospitalization (1.9%) for acute myocardial infarction was low.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
